        [
          "Alderton's Local · Brunch weekend"
        ],
        [],
        [
          "One store's data for a synthetic promotion: an avocado toast kit and a few single-item offers over one weekend. Alderton's is a fictional grocer and every value here is made up for the Safepoint demo."
        ],
        [],
        [
          "Safepoint reads this sheet, calculates demand and margins, asks an agent to propose orders and prices, checks every proposal against the rules, and shows the result for review. It does not write to this sheet."
        ],
        [],
        [
          "Tabs"
        ],
        [
          "Products: what the store sells, with prices, costs, case sizes and shelf life."
        ],
        [
          "Stock: units on hand, reserved and arriving before the promotion, with when they were counted."
        ],
        [
          "Sales: units sold on each of the last four weekends."
        ],
        [
          "Deliveries: each product's supplier, next delivery, order cut-off and any order limit."
        ],
        [
          "Promotion: the brief, the weekend's dates and the kit's price and expected sales."
        ],
        [
          "Kit: what goes into the avocado toast kit."
        ],
        [
          "Offers: each product's role in the promotion and its expected sales lift."
        ],
        [
          "Parameters: limits per category, such as margin floors and maximum discounts."
        ],
        [
          "Rules: the store's rules in plain English. Safepoint turns each into a checked formula that a person approves."
        ],
        [
          "Notes: messages from staff. Safepoint treats them as information, never as instructions."
        ],
        [],
        [
          "Prices are in pounds and quantities in units. Times are UK time, written as a weekday and a time within the promotion week, so the sheet works for any week."
        ],
        [
          "Changes: what a proposal may change, and where each change starts."
        ],
        [
          "Checks: expected outcomes written by the store. Safepoint tests its rules against them; the model drafting the rules never sees this tab."
        ],
        [
          "The timetable row of the Promotion tab states the weekly timing in plain English."
        ]
      ]
